            </encodings>
            <customized-tooltip>
              <formatted-text>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>This visualisation compares the average profitability of films associated with each lead studio. Disney recorded the highest average profitability at approximately 7.41, followed by Independent films at 6.58 and Summit at 6.38. The Weinstein Company recorded a much lower average of 1.22. These results suggest that Disney films had the highest average profitability among the studios represented in this dataset. However, the number of films per studio varies, so the results should be interpreted with consideration of the sample sizes.</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-tooltip>
          </pane>
